    "narrative": "For the August 2nd slate, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.75) stands as our clear centerpiece against a vulnerable Liberatore. While the overall team composition favors speed, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** provides the necessary stability in the middle of the order, benefiting from an 8% boost for his high-leverage spot. **Gunnar Henderson** (67.13) follows closely as our most efficient play; despite facing the formidable Wheeler, **Gunnar Henderson** thrives on a massive 16% park adjustment and a significant platoon advantage, confirming his status as an auto-start regardless of the pitching quality. We are also monitoring **Andy Pages** (62.47) closely; his matchup against Bennett is buoyed by the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which projects to offer high stolen base utility\u2014a key metric for the Austin Waves given our prioritization of speed.\n\nThe bench decision for today was particularly tight, with **Wade Meckler** (35.18) narrowly missing the cut. Despite his sprint speed, the overwhelming strength of Misiorowski (2.07 xERA) effectively neutralized **Wade Meckler**\u2019s potential, dragging his score well below our 40.0 floor. We opted for the higher efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** (61.86), whose favorable matchup against Ritchie provides a better return on investment for our daily efficiency targets. We remain cautious with **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.38) today; while he is in the lineup, his aggressive -15% platoon adjustment serves as a warning that his contribution to the 5x5 categories may be volatile against Alcantara. We will continue to track the health of **Jordan Westburg** and **Jacob Wilson** as we look to rotate the bench for maximum impact throughout the weekend.",
